@{
    Layout = "~/Views/Shared/_Layout.cshtml";
}

<section class="py-4">
    <div class="container">
        <h1 class="mb-3">Understanding Hallucinations</h1>
        <p class="lead">A hallucination occurs when a model generates confident but incorrect information. Identify the causes and build mitigation strategies.</p>

        <div class="card shadow-sm border-0 mb-4">
            <div class="card-body">
                <h2 class="h4">Common Causes</h2>
                <ul>
                    <li>Ambiguous or underspecified prompts.</li>
                    <li>Lack of grounding data or outdated knowledge.</li>
                    <li>Overly creative sampling settings.</li>
                    <li>Model attempting to satisfy strict instructions with limited context.</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="card shadow-sm border-0 mb-4">
            <div class="card-body">
                <h2 class="h4">Mitigation Techniques</h2>
                <ul>
                    <li>Retrieve authoritative context (RAG) before generation.</li>
                    <li>Add verification steps or evaluator prompts.</li>
                    <li>Use structured outputs that can be validated.</li>
                    <li>Adjust temperature and other sampling parameters.</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="alert alert-warning" role="alert">
            <strong>Tip:</strong> Encourage the assistant to say “I don’t know” or “Not enough information” rather than inventing facts.
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
